      "text": "The script fails on current `qiskit-ibm-runtime` for several reasons:\n- `Options` and the V1 `Estimator` call `run(circuits=..., observables=...)` with `.result().values` have been removed.\n- The cloud simulator `ibmq_qasm_simulator` has been retired.\n- `QiskitRuntimeService()` needs saved IBM credentials.\n\nAs the question asks, the fix runs the same Estimator locally on a fake backend:\n- **Backend:** use `FakeManilaV2` from `qiskit_ibm_runtime.fake_provider`. It includes a noise model built from the real device.\n- **Primitive:** switch to `EstimatorV2`. A `Session` given a fake backend runs in local testing mode, so no service is needed.\n- **Circuit and observable:** transpile the circuit for the backend, then map the observable onto the transpiled circuit's layout.\n\n```python\nfrom qiskit import QuantumCircuit, transpile\nfrom qiskit.quantum_info import SparsePauliOp\n# FIX: Options/V1 Estimator and QiskitRuntimeService are removed/unneeded -> import EstimatorV2 and a fake backend, because fake backends run locally in local testing mode\nfrom qiskit_ibm_runtime import Session, EstimatorV2 as Estimator\nfrom qiskit_ibm_runtime.fake_provider import FakeManilaV2\n\nqc = QuantumCircuit(1)\n\nO = SparsePauliOp(['Z'])\n\n# FIX: retired cloud simulator string + service credentials -> FakeManilaV2 instance with ISA transpilation, because local fake backends require ISA circuits and matching observables\nbackend = FakeManilaV2()\nisa_qc = transpile(qc, backend)\nisa_O = O.apply_layout(isa_qc.layout)\n\n# FIX: Session(service=..., backend=str) and V1 run signature -> Session(backend=fake), Estimator(mode=...), PUB-based run and V2 result access, because the V1 API was removed\nwith Session(backend=backend) as session:\n    estimator = Estimator(mode=session)\n    job = estimator.run([(isa_qc, isa_O)])\n    print(job.result()[0].data.evs)\n```",
